            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>In a power conversion system (10) according to one embodiment, a first power converter (11) is connected between a first AC power system (9), and a first DC main line (13A) and a DC return line (13B). A second power converter (12, 15) is connected between the first AC power system (9), and the DC return line (13B) and a second DC main line (13C). Each of the first power converter (11A) and the second power converter (15A) is a modular multilevel converter including a plurality of cascade-connected converter cells (47). Each of the plurality of converter cells (47) includes a plurality of switching elements (61). The power conversion system (10) further comprises: a first control device (33A) to perform pulse-width control on the plurality of switching elements (61) of each of the plurality of converter cells (47) included in the first power converter (11A) according to a first carrier frequency (fc1); and a second control device (34A) to perform the pulse-width control on the plurality of switching elements (61) of each of the plurality of converter cells (47) included in the second power converter (15A) according to a second carrier frequency (fc2) smaller than the first carrier frequency (fc1).</p>
